%N A399030 Irregular triangle read by rows: T(n,k) is the number of transitive relations on n unlabeled points with no isolated point and exactly k related pairs, 1 <= k <= n^2.
%C A399030 Equivalently, the number of arrow-type semigroupoids with n objects and k arrows, up to isomorphism, in the sense of Egri-Nagy and Nehaniv (2025).
%H A399030 Alikhan Sultanbek, <a href="/A399030/b399030.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..385</a>
%H A399030 Gunnar Brinkmann and Brendan D. McKay, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL8/McKay/mckay170.html">Counting unlabelled topologies and transitive relations</a>, J. Int. Seq. 8 (2005), Art. 05.2.1.
%H A399030 Attila Egri-Nagy and Chrystopher L. Nehaniv, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.00837">Computational Exploration of Finite Semigroupoids</a>, arXiv:2509.00837 [cs.FL], 2025.  See Table 1.
%H A399030 Alikhan Sultanbek, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21823492">Source code and complete table to 10 objects</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
